+
+# Long-stay discount for rentals of 3 days or more
+
+Request: reward customers who stay longer. A rental of 3 days or more costs 10% less than its full
+price. Quotes and bookings both show the reduced total.
+
+## Scope
+
+- `quote` and `book` apply the discount when the period covers `n >= 3` whole days: the total is the
+  full price `n * dailyPrice` reduced by 10%.
+  - Rounding: the discounted total is rounded to the nearest euro cent, halves rounded up, so it stays
+    an integer number of euro cents. Computed as `Math.round((full * 9) / 10)`, which avoids
+    floating-point drift.
+  - A period of 1 or 2 days is priced as before, at the full price.
+- The discounted total is what `quote` returns and what `book` returns and stores.
+- `Quote` and `Booking` keep their shape: no extra field is added for the full price.
+- `availability` is unchanged: it does not price anything.
+
+## Acceptance
+
+- A 2-day rental is priced at `2 * dailyPrice`, as before.
+- A 3-day rental is priced at 90% of `3 * dailyPrice`, rounded to the nearest cent, halves up.
+- A longer rental (for example 7 days) is priced at 90% of its full price.
+- `book` returns the same discounted total that `quote` gives for the same period.
+- The total is always an integer number of euro cents.
+- Existing behaviour for period validation, overlap and ids is unchanged.
+
+## Rules applied
+
+1. Money is an integer number of euro cents (the discounted total is rounded to a whole cent).
+2. Times are in UTC, written as ISO-8601 strings.
+3. A booking covers whole days only; the day count drives the discount.
+4. Periods are half-open: `[start, end)`, so the day count is `(end - start) / 1 day`.
+5. The same item cannot be booked twice for overlapping periods.
+
+## Traceability
+
+Request -> this task -> acceptance above -> tests in `src/rental.test.ts`. It extends the pricing rule of
+`task-001-rental-module-basics` (quote = `n * dailyPrice`), which applies to periods under 3 days.
